schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: ROSCA (Rotating Savings and Credit Association)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A savings arrangement where members pool money on a recurring basis and
    take turns receiving the full pot; used in the article to explain and
    legitimate the "member contributions" funding model for regen nodes.
  source_traditions:
    - >-
      Pre-crypto community savings-circle traditions, described in the
      article as having "worked in communities worldwide for generations,
      long before crypto" (e.g. tandas, susus, chit funds, hui — not
      individually named in the source article)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Cited as the real-world precedent that makes a node's small recurring
    member-contribution model ("give what you can," $0-20/month) feel
    familiar and legitimate rather than a crypto-native invention.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Cooperative membership dues (a related but distinct, non-rotating funding pattern)
    - Crypto-native "streaming" contributions (e.g. Superfluid-based recurring
      donations described elsewhere on the site) — same cadence idea, different mechanism
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      A ROSCA rotates the full pooled amount to one member at a time; a
      node's "member contributions" model described in this article does not
      rotate payouts to members — it pools dues to fund the node itself. The
      article invokes ROSCA as a legitimating analogy, not an exact structural
      match.
  tensions:
    - >-
      Using ROSCA as a precedent risks implying more structural similarity to
      the node's funding model than actually exists (see distinction above).
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "ROSCA" as a single, universal pattern flattens real regional and
    cultural variation (tandas, susus, chit funds, hui, etc. differ in rules
    around trust, default risk, and payout order) that the source article
    does not get into.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/funding-your-node.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
